  "result": {
    "text": "To find the largest divisor of a given number n that divides evenly, smaller than n, you can use this approach:\n\n1.  Start checking from the second largest possible number less than n, down to 1.\n2. Check if the current number is a proper divisor of of n.\n3. If it is, return it.\n\nHere's the implementation code of the function:\n\n```python\ndef largest_divisor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\" For a given number n, find the largest number that divides n evenly, smaller than n.\n    >>> largest_divisor(15)\n    5\n    \"\"\"\n    divisor = n - 1\n    while n % divisor != 0:\n        divisor -= 1\n    return divisor\n\n# Example usage:\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    import doctest\n    doctest.testmod()\n```\n\nThis function will correctly find the largest divisor of \\( n \\) that is strictly smaller than \\( n \\).",
